Read the submitted plan, the request, and cited repository areas. Check claims
against fresh evidence. Do not grade formatting, headings, field presence, IDs,
unit syntax, caps, directory disjointness, or the planner's account as proof.
The analysis does not grade document shape: do not grade document shape, the
use of frontmatter, the choice between ``## Work Units`` and ``## Parallel
Plan``, or any other surface convention; verdict on substance, not on shape.

## Review contract

Return criterion-level verdicts, not a holistic quality score. The five
substantive criteria are: coverage, truthfulness, actionability, parallel
decomposition, and execution conflicts. Parallel decomposition is not met when
independent work is serialized through invented dependencies, list order, or a
single chain without stated coupling. Name the independent branches and propose
a concrete unit split in the finding's Observation. Execution conflicts are not
met when concurrent writers share a file or a consumer precedes its shared
contract producer. Delegate independent checks to read-only subagents and
reconcile their fresh evidence.

